    "created_at": "2023-07-05T16:51:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-05T16:51:31Z",
    "body": "> I think the first test in html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/initial-empty-document/window-open-history-length.html does check this?\r\n\r\nChrome reports 0 for these. Gecko with my patch from https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=543435 reports 0 as well as a consequence of the high-level change without trying to target this test specifically. This makes me wish to change the test expectation to 0.\r\n\r\n\"Shippable\"-configuration builds with today's iteration of my Gecko patch [are available](https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=4e3507c2ce82a6b42db5793694eb97eb7fd0607c).\r\n\r\nIs the mechanism by which Safari says 1 known?\r\n\r\n",
